WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.403
SPEAKER:<i> In 2002,
 FBI and CIA agents</i>

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:07.774
<i> thought they had nabbed a
diabolical al-Qaeda mastermind.</i>

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.342
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.145
<i> Abu Zubaydah has never been
 charged with a crime.</i>

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:16.015
SPEAKER 2:<i> He was imprisoned
 in the secret CIA unit</i>

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.617
<i> called Strawberry Fields.</i>

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:21.154
<i> As in, forever.</i>

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:27.427
SPEAKER 3:
<i> Prior to 9/11, the CIA never
 captured or detained anybody.</i>

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.827
They weren't prepared.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:33.266
People started looking for
who was best to interrogate,
and there weren't any.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.103
SPEAKER:
<i>Psychologist James Mitchell was
 the only candidate considered.</i>

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:39.772 line:0%
<i>I just took it for granted that
they knew what they were doing.</i>

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.610
SPEAKER 2:<i> CIA officers were
 certain he was holding back,</i>

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.045
<i> because he wasn't telling them
 what they wanted to hear.</i>

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.614
Something more aggressive
had to be done.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:54.220
The lawyer's philosophy is,
"Tell me what you wanna do,
boss, and I'll make it legal."

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.723
We asked him to draw
what was done to him.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.159
SPEAKER 4:<i> Abu Zubaydah
 is put in isolation.</i>

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:02.962
SPEAKER 5:
<i> Everything that was happening
 was Mitchell's experiment.</i>

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:04.464
<i> Nudity has been approved,</i>

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.465
<i> sleep deprivation
 has been approved,</i>

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:07.801
<i> noise has been approved.</i>

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.369
The same song
again and again and again.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.638
SPEAKER 4:<i> He spent 11 days
 in a coffin-shaped box.</i>

00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:14.140
<i> He was on the waterboard.</i>

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:16.476
I mean, this is crazy.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.412
SPEAKER 2:<i> The best evidence
 of what happened is the video.</i>

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.880
SPEAKER 6:<i> What was
 the reason why you thought</i>

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.681
<i> that it was important
 to have the tapes destroyed?</i>

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:25.484 line:0%
<i> I needed to protect
 the people who were there.</i>

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:28.487
Destroying evidence
would inevitably lead

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.022
<i> to accusations of a cover up.</i>

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.258 line:0%
<i>It would make the CIA look bad.</i>

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:35.161
SPEAKER:<i> It was
 an impossible story to tell,</i>

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:38.197
<i> so I sued the CIA
 to get materials unredacted.</i>

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.700
SPEAKER 4:<i> We saw constant
 manipulation by the CIA.</i>

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.736
<i> Misleading Bush,
 misleading Obama.</i>

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.371
JAMES MITCHELL:
<i>If my boss tells me it's legal,</i>

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.674
<i> if the president approved it,
 I'm not gonna get into</i>

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.509
what some journalist
thinks about it.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.579
In America,
we have this thing called
"innocent until proven guilty."

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:58.017
We were the leaders
of the effort against
cruel and unusual punishment.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.553
<i> After 9/11,
 that's out the window.</i>

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.921
SPEAKER 2:<i> Do the ends
 always justify the means?</i>

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.391
<i> Are we prepared
 to abandon our principles</i>

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.260
<i> in order to defend them?</i>

